# nr-office-ooxml-package: integration fragment

The crate mixdog-ooxml (native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml) is new: the portable OOXML engine (XML string helpers, the package
container, content types and relationships, blank packages, worksheet cells, pptx shape relationships, the legacy-file
check, template tokens, the placeholder scan, the document fingerprint). Later tasks add one module per Node file.
No protocol method, service or SERVICE_PENDING name belongs to it.

## native/core/Cargo.toml

In [workspace] members, add (beside "crates/mixdog-ooxml-text"):

    "crates/mixdog-ooxml",

In [workspace.dependencies], add (beside mixdog-ooxml-text):

    mixdog-ooxml = { path = "crates/mixdog-ooxml" }

Every dependency of the crate is already a workspace entry (mixdog-fsio, mixdog-js, mixdog-office-base, mixdog-ooxml-text,
serde_json, sha1, sha2, zip; dev: base64, tempfile, mixdog-office-base with feature test-support). The crate lists
mixdog-workspace-hack itself; if the hakari manifest is regenerated, include mixdog-ooxml.

## native/core/Cargo.lock

Add the package entry (cargo adds it itself on the first --locked-less build; the dependency names are):
mixdog-ooxml: base64, mixdog-fsio, mixdog-js, mixdog-office-base, mixdog-ooxml-text, mixdog-workspace-hack, serde_json,
sha1, sha2, tempfile, zip.

## native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json

In the "sets" list, after the entry of office-measure (keep the list sorted by set name), add:

    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-package.mjs --tree <tree>",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-package/MANIFEST.json",
      "manifestSha256": "f36f69eae1e1be744b88b8319c5f76e57787a180a8858ef10c1da1301b219a2e",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-package.mjs",
      "set": "office-package",
      "totalBytes": 133067
    }

(Recompute manifestSha256 and totalBytes from the committed office-package/MANIFEST.json and golden.json if the tool that
keeps this file reorders or reformats them.)

## Not compiled

The crate was written without cargo (the wave is compiled by the lead): the first build of mixdog-ooxml and its tests,
cargo test -p mixdog-ooxml, is the check. The twin test tests/twin_package.rs replays native/core/fixtures/office-package
and needs no Node; twin_live_package (ignored) re-records through Node.
